      "# Feedbacks vocabulary and selection\n\n| User language                                                              | Meaning and action                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| feedback, issue, bug, task, ticket, thread, review, “feedbacks mein dekho” | A Feedbacks discussion thread here. An issue does not mean GitHub unless specified.                                                                                                                                   |\n| pin, point, annotation, marking, comment on an element, “yeh wala point”   | An entry in `context.annotations`; use its UUID. Display numbers are capture-local, not IDs. A legacy single anchor may have no annotation ID: resolve the thread, never invent an ID.                                |\n| comment, reply, discussion                                                 | Original body or a named reply. One message can describe several tasks; do not silently close them all.                                                                                                               |\n| screenshot, SS, capture, full page, point image                            | A private asset. Read metadata and actual pixels; filenames are insufficient.                                                                                                                                         |\n| recording, video, clip                                                     | Video evidence with an authenticated URL. A thumbnail is not playback.                                                                                                                                                |\n| page, screen, URL, mobile/desktop                                          | Filter reviewed URL/device; a Feedbacks app URL selects feedback, not the reviewed page.                                                                                                                              |\n| today, aaj, abhi, new                                                      | Establish timezone and submission versus activity. `createdAfter`/`createdBefore` filter creation; `activityAfter` includes updates to old threads. Today is local midnight to next midnight, not a rolling 24 hours. |\n| my feedback, Suyog's issues, reviewer name                                 | Resolve a unique stable author ID. Token owner, agent and human requester can differ; clarify ambiguous names.                                                                                                        |\n| top priority, urgent, first                                                | Explicit flags lead. Weighted priority requires policy access. Separate stored ranking from a proposed dependency/effort order.                                                                                       |\n| pending, unresolved, remaining                                             | Usually work not resolved/declined. `workState` selects an exact state. New replies can need follow-up even after resolution.                                                                                         |\n| answered, responded                                                        | Discussion dimension; not fixed/resolved.                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| fixed, done, resolve                                                       | Verify agreed scope/evidence and mutate only authorized points/threads. Tests alone do not prove deployment.                                                                                                          |\n| remove, delete, dismiss                                                    | Clarify: removed point, archived thread, declined work and permanent deletion differ. Done never means delete.                                                                                                        |\n| likes, support, votes                                                      | Anonymous unique thread/reply/view counts. Voter identities are intentionally unavailable.                                                                                                                            |\n| GitHub/Jira/Linear issue                                                   | Optional external association. Read provenance; do not create or message externally without authorization.                                                                                                            |\n\nFor “today's feedback, make a plan”, return counts and proposed order first, then discuss execution. Empty results mean only the stated filters/scopes returned no matches.\n\n- **Assigned / claimed / kaun kaam kar raha hai:** Read `assignments.list`. A claim identifies the Feedbacks member, named agent, thread and optional point IDs, plus a two-hour renewable expiry. Thread status alone does not identify a worker. Disjoint points may have different agents; overlapping active claims conflict.\n- **My current work / abhi main X par work kar raha hoon:** The member profile's `currentWork` is a broad one-line focus. It is advisory context, separate from an active thread/point claim.\n- **Shared Codex/Claude account:** A model-provider subscription, never the Feedbacks employee identity. Use separate personal Feedbacks keys. Account quota does not establish task ownership or correctness.\n",
